BENCH / TOPOLOGY AS TESTED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Single L3 DUT = u4  S/N 264A23052  MAC 84e3.2787.09c0.
      subnet A : vlan10  10.10.10.0/27  (SVI 10.10.10.2)   - sender side
      subnet B : vlan20  10.10.20.0/27  (SVI 10.10.20.1)   - directed-broadcast target,
                 `ip directed-broadcast` enabled
  Host = tb470 eth2 -> u4 port1.0.2 (802.1Q trunk, vlans 10+20):
      eth2.10 = 10.10.10.20/27 (sender, subnet A)
      eth2.20 = 10.10.20.20/27 (receiver, subnet B)

METHOD / SCOPE
  No IXIA. The two frames are crafted with scapy on eth2.10 (subnet A): both are addressed
  to the subnet-B directed-broadcast IP 10.10.20.31, one with L2 dst = u4's vlan10 SVI MAC
  (84:e3:27:87:09:c0), one with L2 dst = ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff. Delivery onto subnet B is
  captured with tcpdump on eth2.20. Functional test.

